examples.solution_text:
Draw $A$ and $B$ from Start because neither has an immediate predecessor.

Draw $C$ after $A$ and $D$ after $B$. Join the ends of $C$ and $D$ at the vertex where $E$ starts: $E$ must wait for both.

Draw $F$ after $E$, ending at Finish.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},every path/.style={line width=0.7pt}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (2,1.3);
\coordinate (Q) at (2,-1.3);
\coordinate (R) at (4,0);
\coordinate (T) at (6,0);
\coordinate (Z) at (8,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(P) node[midway,above left] {$A,3$};
\draw[->] (S)--(Q) node[midway,below left] {$B,4$};
\draw[->] (P)--(R) node[midway,above right] {$C,2$};
\draw[->] (Q)--(R) node[midway,below right] {$D,5$};
\draw[->] (R)--(T) node[midway,above] {$E,6$};
\draw[->] (T)--(Z) node[midway,above] {$F,2$};
\foreach \v in {S,P,Q,R,T,Z}{\fill (\v) circle (2pt);}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};
\node[right] at (Z) {Finish};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Draw $A$, $B$ and $C$ from Start, with separate end vertices.

$D$ needs $A$ and $B$, while $E$ needs $B$ and $C$. Keep the end of $B$ separate and draw a dummy from it to each of the other two end vertices.

Draw $D$ from the vertex reached by $A$ and the first dummy. Draw $E$ from the vertex reached by $C$ and the second dummy. Both activities end at Finish.

The dashed edges pass the dependency on $B$ to both activities. Each has duration $0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},every path/.style={line width=0.7pt}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3,2);
\coordinate (Q) at (3,0);
\coordinate (R) at (3,-2);
\coordinate (Z) at (6,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(P) node[midway,above left] {$A,7$};
\draw[->] (S)--(Q) node[midway,above] {$B,4$};
\draw[->] (S)--(R) node[midway,below left] {$C,6$};
\draw[->,dashed] (Q)--(P) node[midway,right] {dummy, $0$};
\draw[->,dashed] (Q)--(R) node[midway,right] {dummy, $0$};
\draw[->] (P)--(Z) node[midway,above right] {$D,8$};
\draw[->] (R)--(Z) node[midway,below right] {$E,9$};
\foreach \v in {S,P,Q,R,Z}{\fill (\v) circle (2pt);}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};
\node[right] at (Z) {Finish};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

